<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Physician-scientist exploring genomics, AI, and computational biology"
	pubDate={new Date('December 06 2024')}
>
	<h2>Background</h2>
	<p>
		I'm an ophthalmologist (M.D.) turned PhD researcher at KAIST, working on glioblastoma genomics
		and computational biology. My research focuses on tumor evolution and therapeutic target discovery
		using CRISPR screens, single-cell analysis, and AI-powered data analysis.
	</p>

	<h2>Research Interests</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Glioblastoma tumor evolution and cellular plasticity</li>
		<li>CRISPR-based functional genomics</li>
		<li>Single-cell and spatial transcriptomics</li>
		<li>AI-augmented research workflows</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What I Write About</h2>
	<p>
		This blog documents my journey as a physician-scientist: research insights, technical tutorials
		on bioinformatics and AI tools, and reflections on building systems that amplify research output.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Find me on <a href="https://github.com/JiehoonKwak">GitHub</a> or reach out via email.
	</p>
